## 🚀 Bubble Sort — **Optimized Version (Adaptive)**

👉 Stops early if already sorted.

### Code
```c
#include <stdio.h>

void bubbleSortOptimized(int a[], int n) {
    int i, j, temp, swapped;
    for(i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        swapped = 0;
        for(j = 0; j < n-1-i; j++) {
            if(a[j] > a[j+1]) {
                temp = a[j];
                a[j] = a[j+1];
                a[j+1] = temp;
                swapped = 1;
            }
        }
        if(swapped == 0)
            break;
    }
}

int main() {
    int a[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}; // Already sorted
    int n = sizeof(a)/sizeof(a[0]);

    bubbleSortOptimized(a, n);

    printf("Sorted: ");
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
        printf("%d ", a[i]);
}
```

